<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shibi Khagan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 619</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shibi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khagan">Khagan</a> was ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-turkic-khaganate">Eastern Turkic Khaganate</a> from 609 to 619. He turned against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sui-dynasty">Sui dynasty</a> and in 615 besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-yang-of-sui">Emperor Yang of Sui</a> at Yanmen, in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. During the Sui collapse he backed several Chinese rebels and exacted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">silk</a> and tribute, making the Eastern Turks the strongest power on China's northern frontier.</p></div>
